        "original_id": "766752ef-3230-5a81-a8c1-907235aef147",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anaïs Nin, Odysseas Elytis\n- Works: The Four-Chambered Heart, Cities of the Interior\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Concepts: Romantic modernism\n\nFacts:\n- Anaïs Nin was born as Angela Anaïs Juana Antolina Rosa Edelmira Nin y Culmell on February 21, 1903.\n- Anaïs Nin was born in France to Cuban parents and was also raised in France.\n- Odysseas Elytis, the pen name of Odysseas Alepoudellis, was born on November 2, 1911.\n- Odysseas Elytis was regarded as a major exponent of romantic modernism in Greece and internationally.\n- The Four-Chambered Heart is a 1950 autobiographical novel by French-born writer Anaïs Nin.\n- The Four-Chambered Heart is part of Anaïs Nin's Cities of the Interior sequence.\n- Odysseas Elytis received the 1979 Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- Anaïs Nin died on January 14, 1977.\n- Odysseas Elytis died on March 18, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
